<title>USA: Pharmaceutical Formulations files NDA.</title>
<headline>Pharmaceutical Formulations files NDA.</headline>
<dateline>EDISON, N.J. 1996-10-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pharmaceutical Formulations Inc said on Friday that it filed abbreviated New Drug Applications with the U.S. Food and Drug Administration for three new drugs.</p>
<p>The company said it filed applications for its acid reducer Cimetidine, analgesic Naproxen Sodium and Sucralfate, a generic version of a drug used to treat duodenal ulcers.  </p>
<p>Cimetidine was a generic version of SmithKline Beecham Plc's Tagamet, used to treat heartburn and acid indigestion. Naproxen was a generic version of Roche Holding Ltd's Alleve and Sucralfate was a generic version of Hoechst Marion Roussel Inc's Carafate.</p>
